WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:16.354
Unit sixteen: Adverbial Clauses. Today you will explain reasons, time and contrast with subordinate clauses.

4
00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:19.423
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.460
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.364
Because.

7
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.233
Because means for the reason that.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.524
I stayed because it rained.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.839
Your turn. Say: Because.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.713
Because.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.312
Since.

12
00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:42.595
Since means because, or from a time.

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:44.579
Since you're here, help me.

14
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:47.383
Your turn. Say: Since.

15
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.246
Since.

16
00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:52.706
As.

17
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:55.612
As means because, or while.

18
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:57.938
As it was late, we left.

19
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.680
Your turn. Say: As.

20
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:04.244
As.

21
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:05.741
While.

22
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.320
While means during the time that.

23
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:10.545
While I cooked, she read.

24
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.814
Your turn. Say: While.

25
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.598
While.

26
00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:19.339
Whereas.

27
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.570
Whereas means used to show contrast.

28
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.160
He is tall, whereas she is short.

29
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.368
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

30
00:01:31.233 --> 00:01:32.083
Whereas.

31
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.176
Reason clause.

32
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:37.659
Reason clause means a clause giving a reason.

33
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.750
A reason clause.

34
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.118
Your turn. Say: Reason clause.

35
00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:47.525
Reason clause.

36
00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:49.412
Time clause.

37
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:52.869
Time clause means a clause giving time.

38
00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:54.856
A time clause.

39
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.137
Your turn. Say: Time clause.

40
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.338
Time clause.

41
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:04.526
Contrast clause.

42
00:02:05.517 --> 00:02:08.387
Contrast clause means a clause showing contrast.

43
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:10.611
A contrast clause.

44
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:14.461
Your turn. Say: Contrast clause.

45
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.800
Contrast clause.

46
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.146
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:26.645
Visal, give a reason for something you did today.

48
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:38.265
I took a taxi because it was raining. A clause of reason answers why. Because, since and as introduce it, but as and since are more formal and usually start the sentence.

49
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.315
What about time and contrast?

50
00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:59.491
Time: while, when, as soon as, before, after. While I was cooking, she read. Contrast: whereas and while: My brother is tall, whereas I am short.

51
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.211
Where does the clause go?

52
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:16.981
Before or after the main clause. If it comes first, we use a comma: Since you are here, help me. If it comes second, we usually have no comma. A subordinate clause cannot stand alone.

53
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.587
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.818
Grammar focus: Adverbial clauses: reason, time, contrast.

55
00:03:25.118 --> 00:03:26.258
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.147
Because it was raining, I took a taxi.

57
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.200
While I was cooking, she was reading.

58
00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:35.209
He is tall, whereas I am short.

59
00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:44.095
Because / since / as = reason. While / when / as soon as = time. Whereas / while = contrast. A clause at the start takes a comma.

60
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.234
Be careful! Don't say: Because it was raining, so I left.

61
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.513
Say: Because it was raining, I left.

62
00:03:52.813 --> 00:03:54.604
Do not use because and so.

63
00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.099
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.273
Why, When, Whereas.

65
00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.234
I took a taxi because it was raining heavily.

66
00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:07.115
Since you are here, please help me with the dishes.

67
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.274
While I was cooking, my sister was reading.

68
00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.940
My brother is tall, whereas I am rather short.

69
00:04:14.933 --> 00:04:17.746
A reason clause explains why something happened.

70
00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:22.707
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.422
blank it was late, we went home.

72
00:04:25.722 --> 00:04:29.549
A, As. B, Whereas. C, Unless.

73
00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.774
The answer is A: As.

74
00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:38.648
He loves tea, blank I prefer coffee.

75
00:04:38.948 --> 00:04:42.752
A, because. B, whereas. C, since.

76
00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.102
The answer is B: whereas.

77
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.331
I stayed home blank I felt sick.

78
00:04:51.631 --> 00:04:55.168
A, because. B, whereas. C, while.

79
00:04:58.733 --> 00:05:00.861
The answer is A: because.

80
00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:03.494
Which shows time?

81
00:05:03.794 --> 00:05:08.213
A, while I was cooking. B, because it rained. C, whereas she left.

82
00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.022
The answer is A: while I was cooking.

83
00:05:15.183 --> 00:05:18.715
According to the reading, why did the writer take a taxi?

84
00:05:19.015 --> 00:05:22.843
A, it was raining. B, it was late. C, it was cheap.

85
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.260
The answer is A: it was raining.

86
00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:32.607
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:36.181
Write a sentence with an adverbial clause of reason.

88
00:05:44.983 --> 00:05:46.553
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:46.853 --> 00:05:56.625
I took the bus because my bicycle was broken. Since it was raining, I also took an umbrella. The clause of reason answers the question why.

90
00:05:56.925 --> 00:05:58.588
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.483 --> 00:06:05.758
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverbial clauses: reason, time, contrast.

92
00:06:06.058 --> 00:06:10.881
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

93
00:06:11.181 --> 00:06:14.089
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.389 --> 00:06:16.844
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

